# Copies and returns the selected string without permanently changing the clipboard
# (the clipboard is saved before and restored afterwards).
## @? clipboardSaved as Binary might be better — would preserve non-text clipboard content (images, formatted data), not just plain text

Paste from clipboard clipboardSaved ## save clipboard — unfortunately only works for plain text in the clipboard

# clear clipboard, by copying an empty string to
Calculate clipboard as ''
Copy to clipboard clipboard

Standard menu command *Edit/11003 {Copy}
Paste from clipboard clipboard

Copy to clipboard clipboardSaved ## restore clipboard

If clipboard=200 ## error code
	Calculate clipboard as ''
End If

Quit method clipboard